## 4. Cross-package `@seealso` (roxygen)

Add `@seealso` links across packages so the reference pages form a web. Examples:

```r
# curveRfreq::fit_calibration_freq()
#' @seealso [curveRcore::preprocess_standards()] for the upstream preprocessing,
#'   [curveRcore::assess_model_eligibility()] for the gating logic,
#'   [curveRbayes::fit_calibration_bayes()] for the Bayesian alternative with an
#'   identical output structure.

# curveRweights::fit_precision_weights()   (only valid AFTER Issue 1)
#' @seealso [curveRfreq::fit_calibration_freq_multiplate()] /
#'   [curveRbayes::fit_calibration_bayes()] to produce the calibration_result_multiplate
#'   that [as_weight_data()] consumes.
```

Links *to* `curveRweights` are only correct once Issue 1 has finalized its API — another reason the
weights pieces come after Issue 1.

