## 5. Per-spoke CI/CD

Each repo gets the standard `r-lib/actions` pkgdown workflow that builds and deploys to its own
`gh-pages` on push to `main` and on tags. (The hub's cross-repo *rebuild-on-spoke-release* dispatch
workflow is Issue 3 — don't build it here.) Confirm `R-CMD-check` passes on the runners too;
broken roxygen/examples will fail the reference build.

---

## 6. Suggested execution order within Issue 2

1. `curveRcore` first — it has no internal deps and defines the classes every other site links to;
   getting its reference pages live means the others' `@seealso` cross-links resolve.
2. `curveRfreq`, then `curveRbayes`.
3. `curveRweights` rebuild last (consumes the Issue-1 API; its vignette references the others).

